recent proposals to expand and reform  the child tax credit  have gained significant attention in  congress when considering such reforms  it's important to understand the tax  benefits currently available  the federal income tax provides a number  of family tax benefits  including the head of household filing  status and tax credits for children  and child care expenses in 2021  the total value of these benefits is 209  billion dollars  and the average benefit per household  with children is almost  4 600 this includes a 2 000  partially refundable child tax credit  the distribution of these benefits is  highly progressive meaning that lower  income households  receive a larger benefit relative to  their income than higher income  households  current proposals would increase the  child tax credit and make the credit  fully refundable meaning the credits  available regardless of income  therefore these proposals all reduce  poverty rates unfortunately  by eliminating the phase-in of the  credit these proposals would also raise  marginal tax rates on work  for low-income households with children  should congress expand the child tax  credit  let us know in our poll also let us know  what other topics  you'd like our scholars to cover in 60  seconds and be sure to like and  subscribe  for more research and videos from aei
 

